---
// src/pages/wasm-studio.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import WasmStudio from '../components/WasmStudio.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="⚙️ WebAssembly Cryptographic & Document Processing Studio"
  description="Client-side WebAssembly suite for cryptographic SHA-256 hash generation, CSP whitelist calculations, and OKF v0.2 document processing."
  slug="wasm-studio"
>
  <h1>⚙️ WebAssembly Cryptographic & Document Processing Studio</h1>
  <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--lab-muted, #64748b); line-height: 1.6;">
    Welcome to the <strong>CMSForNerd2</strong> client-side WebAssembly (Wasm) studio. This module demonstrates browser-native, zero-server execution of cryptographic hashing, Content Security Policy (CSP) whitelist generation, Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2 document structure parsing, and in-browser WebAssembly vector embeddings with FastMCP semantic AI search.
  </p>

  <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--lab-border, #e2e8f0); margin: 1.5rem 0;" />

  <section>
    <h2>🔐 Client-Side Cryptographic Hashing & CSP Whitelisting</h2>
    <p>
      In high-security static site deployments, inline scripts and critical assets must be whitelisted using cryptographic SHA-256 digests in HTTP Content Security Policy (<code>Content-Security-Policy</code>) headers.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Zero External API Calls:</strong> Text strings and script contents are hashed locally using hardware-accelerated SHA-256 instructions.</li>
      <li><strong>Deterministic Whitelisting:</strong> Produces Base64-encoded digests matching Nginx and Cloudflare CSP whitelist formats (<code>'sha256-...'</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Integrity Assurance:</strong> Ensures content tamper-proofing before static deployment.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
    <h2>📄 Client-Side OKF v0.2 Document Processing</h2>
    <p>
      The Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2 standard requires machine-readable YAML frontmatter carrying trust and freshness pillars (<code>spec_version</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>timestamp</code>, <code>topics</code>).
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Schema Validation:</strong> Checks for required frontmatter fields.</li>
      <li><strong>Word & Line Metrics:</strong> Performs tokenisation and line frequency analysis.</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy Guaranteed:</strong> Content never leaves your local browser memory space.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
    <h2>🧠 Offline In-Browser WebAssembly Vector Embeddings & FastMCP Semantic Search</h2>
    <p>
      For isolated, air-gapped offline environments, the studio executes normalized 384-dimensional vector embedding models natively inside browser Web Workers, persisting vectors to IndexedDB and routing search through FastMCP tool schemas.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Web Worker Isolation Layer:</strong> Offloads heavy matrix multiplications (e.g. Transformers.js / ONNX feature extraction) from the UI thread.</li>
      <li><strong>IndexedDB Local Storage:</strong> Stores raw document snippets alongside 384-dimensional Float32 vector embeddings locally in the browser.</li>
      <li><strong>FastMCP Semantic Search Protocol:</strong> Wraps mathematical cosine similarity matching inside the <code>semantic_code_search</code> tool schema for internal RAG pipelines.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
    <h2>📡 Service Worker Link Prefetching & Offline Fallback Handlers</h2>
    <p>
      Next-gen Progressive Web App (PWA) resilience in CMSForNerd2 pairs Workbox runtime caching and speculative client link prefetching with automatic network offline fallback handlers.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Speculative Viewport Link Prefetching:</strong> Detects internal links in viewport or touch interactions and pre-populates the Service Worker <code>pages-cache</code> before navigation.</li>
      <li><strong>Automatic Offline Fallback:</strong> Serves the statically compiled <code>/offline/</code> fallback route seamlessly when network connectivity drops and uncached routes are requested.</li>
      <li><strong>Network Awareness:</strong> Dynamically adapts theme and status indicators based on real-time browser connection state.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <WasmStudio />

  <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--lab-border, #e2e8f0); margin: 1.5rem 0;" />

  <footer>
    <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; opacity: 0.7;">
      <em>Deep State of Mind (DSOM) For My AI Protocol | Harisfazillah Jamel (LinuxMalaysia) | 2026-09-06</em><br />
      <em>Standard: UK English | DBP-standard Bahasa Melayu Malaysia (Piawai) | GNU General Public License v3.0</em>
    </p>
  </footer>
</Layout>
